✅ 1. Business Login
Goal: Each vendor/business should have its own secure account.
Implementation:
Business registration and login (email/phone + password or OTP).


Role-based access (Admin, Staff, Viewer).


JWT or OAuth2 authentication.


Each business gets its own isolated database schema or tenant ID.


Handled: ✔️ Multi-tenant architecture.

✅ 2. Inventory (Vegetables/Fruits, etc.)
Goal: Manage all inventory items — fruits, vegetables, etc.
Implementation:
Inventory table with fields:


item_id, name, category, unit (kg, box, lot), price, current_stock.


Add, update, delete items (CRUD).


Auto-update on every sale or purchase.


Support for different units (kgs, lots, boxes).


Handled: ✔️ Add/update items, auto inventory tracking.

✅ 3. Customer Onboarding
Goal: Register and manage customers easily.
Fields:
Name


Contact Number


Aadhar (optional or encrypted)


Address


Photo (upload)


Opening balance / Crate balance


Implementation:
Customer table linked to Business ID.


Photo upload via storage (AWS S3 / Firebase).


Option to scan Aadhaar QR for quick onboarding.


Handled: ✔️ Full onboarding with identification.

✅ 4. Patti Book Entry Form (Transactions CRUD)
Goal: Record and manage daily transactions.
Fields:
Customer


Item


Quantity/Weight (Box, Lot, Kg/Gm)


Price per unit


Date/Time


Notes


Payment Mode (Cash, UPI, Credit)


Implementation:
Transaction table linked to:


Customer ID


Item ID


Business ID


CRUD operations with validations.


Auto-update inventory + crate count.


Handled: ✔️ Full CRUD on transaction entries.

✅ 5. Customer Receipts
Goal: Generate and print digital receipts for each transaction.
Features:
Auto-generate PDF receipt after each Patti entry.


Include:


Business name/logo


Customer details


Items list


Total, discounts, taxes


Balance amount


Crate summary


Option to:


Print directly


Send via WhatsApp/email


Handled: ✔️ Printable and digital receipts.

✅ 6. Search, Filter & History
Goal: Easily find customer data and past transactions.
Features:
Search by name or phone number.


Filter by date range.


View last few transactions per customer.


“Recent Activity” widget on dashboard.


Handled: ✔️ Search + filtering tools for usability.

✅ 7. Receivable / Balance Amount Tracking
Goal: Know how much each customer owes.
Features:
Auto-update outstanding balance per transaction.


Track:


Credit sales


Payments received


Separate “Receivables” report showing:


Customer name


Balance amount


Last transaction date


Handled: ✔️ Automated balance tracking.

✅ 8. Customer Reports & Dashboards
Goal: Summarize all customer-related data visually.
Features:
Transaction count, total spend, average purchase value.


Crate summary (Taken vs Returned).


Balance due.


Graphs for trends over time.


Handled: ✔️ Customer-level dashboards.

✅ 9. Sales Receipts (Daily Summary)
Goal: View all sales of all customers on a given day.
Features:
Generate daily report by date.


Export/print sales summary.


Include:


Total sales of transactions


Total crates out


Payments received


Handled: ✔️ Sales report and receipts per day.

✅ 10. Sales Dashboard
Goal: Business overview dashboard.
Features:
Total revenue this week/month.


Top-selling items.


Crates in/out summary.


Outstanding receivables.


Forecasted sales and stock.


Handled: ✔️ Business analytics and forecasting.

✅ 11. Crate Reports
Goal: Track crates given and returned for each customer.
Implementation:
Crate table linked to customer:


crate_id, customer_id, crates_given, crates_returned, balance.


Auto-update after each transaction or crate return entry.


Alerts for pending returns.


Handled: ✔️ Real-time crate balance tracking.

✅ 12. Credit History
Goal: Maintain detailed payment and credit record.
Features:
Record every credit/debit adjustment.


Link to transactions.


Show credit timeline per customer.


Optional credit limit enforcement.


Handled: ✔️ Transparent credit tracking.

✅ 13. Online Software (Cloud-Based)
Goal: Always accessible, secure, and synced.
Implementation:
Cloud-hosted (AWS / Firebase / GCP).


Role-based multi-login.


Progressive Web App (PWA) for offline mode.


Daily automatic backups.


Handled: ✔️ Fully online, reliable, and portable.

✅ 14. Forecast & Wastage Minimization
Goal: Predict stock needs and minimize waste.
Implementation:
Use historical sales to:


Predict demand.


Flag overstocked items.


Recommend reorder levels.


Handled: ✔️ Data-driven forecasting (AI-ready).

✅ 15. Data Migration & Backfill
Goal: Ensure seamless transition and no data loss.
Implementation:
Bulk upload CSV/Excel for existing data.


Migration scripts for legacy formats.


Backup + restore mechanism.


Change logs and data audit trail.


Handled: ✔️ Secure migration and data integrity.

